---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Scenario E — Artifact spine — Querial Labs" active="e">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Scenario E</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Artifact spine</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                Full produce → transform → consume path. One structural root. DuckDB
                <code class="text-foreground">artifact-sql</code> between extracts and
                dual staged sinks (SQL Server and PostgreSQL). SS staged MERGE scripts
                are real steps here (promoted from C’s reference files).
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/scenario-e-artifacts.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download scenario-e-artifacts.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/run-through" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Load and test
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/devops-artifacts" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Artifacts docs
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>Why this lab</h2>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full text-sm">
                    <thead>
                        <tr class="text-left border-b border-border/50">
                            <th class="py-2 pr-3">Lab</th>
                            <th class="py-2">Focus</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/30"><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-medium text-foreground">B</td><td>Minimal PG: extract → staged PG</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/30"><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-medium text-foreground">C</td><td>Multi-root; SS sql_command + PG staged</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/30"><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-medium text-foreground">D</td><td>Single-root fan-out + continue on SS</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-medium text-foreground">E</td><td>Extract → artifact-sql → dual staged sinks</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h2>Package</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package <code class="text-foreground">aw-scenario-e</code>, pipeline <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_e</code>.</li>
                <li>Three stubs: <code class="text-foreground">aw-source</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-sql-dest</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Topology</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>extract_sales_order (ROOT, parquet)
  ├─(artifact_available)→ transform_sales_order (artifact-sql, DuckDB)
  │                         ├─(artifact_available)→ load_sales_order_sqlserver (staged)
  │                         └─(artifact_available)→ load_sales_order_postgres (staged)
  └─(succeeded)→ extract_sales_line
                   └─(artifact_available)→ transform_sales_line (artifact-sql)
                                             ├─→ load_sales_line_sqlserver (staged)
                                             └─→ load_sales_line_postgres (staged)

Line loads also require the matching order load (required) on each destination.</code></pre>
            <p>
                Line extract hangs off the order extract so the graph stays single-root
                (unlike C). All artifact edges use <code class="text-foreground">artifact_available</code>.
            </p>

            <h2>artifact-sql config</h2>
            <p>
                Transforms have <code class="text-foreground">config.outputName</code>
                (<code class="text-foreground">sales_order_transformed</code> /
                <code class="text-foreground">sales_line_transformed</code>) and
                <code class="text-foreground">config.inputs.&lt;name&gt;.from_step</code>.
                DuckDB SQL references inputs with the package token form
                <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input.name }}"}</code>.
                Eligible agents run DuckDB embedded — not a separate warehouse you manage.
                <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> is same-run only and requires
                the producer Succeeded.
            </p>
            <p>
                Staged sinks bind <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> to the
                transform, not the extract. Column contracts match the transformed schema.
                <code class="text-foreground">transaction.mode: stage-and-execute</code>.
            </p>

            <h2>Flags (required)</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:Artifacts=true</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:DuckDb=true</code></li>
            </ul>
            <p>Both destinations use staged handlers, so both flags apply even for the SQL Server half.</p>

            <h2>Walkthrough extras</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li>Import, resolve all three connections, Development endpoints on each.</li>
                <li>Publish: one root — no multi-root warning.</li>
                <li>Deployment: <code class="text-foreground">before_run</code> migrations, Development, activate, trigger.</li>
                <li>Run Graph: watch extract → transform (DuckDB) → both sinks. Inspector artifacts on transform and on each load. SQL tab shows published DuckDB and staged MERGE, not the draft.</li>
                <li>If a sink fails after transforms succeeded, failed-cone retry can reuse succeeded steps and clone artifacts (DevOps on run details).</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Verify</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_order;
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_line;</code></pre>
            <p>Run on both destinations. Counts should match each other after a healthy run (same transformed grain).</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
